01:22.500 --> 01:26.180
Well, let's delve into the fascinating world of cryptographic algorithms

01:26.820 --> 01:32.700
Specifically RSA or revest Shamir Edelman. This algorithm is a cornerstone of modern

01:33.180 --> 01:39.060
Cryptography and it owes its strength to the enigmatic nature of prime numbers. Here's how it works

01:39.740 --> 01:45.360
RSA uses two large prime numbers and multiplies them together to create an encryption key

01:45.660 --> 01:48.220
